From 5e05bfbc9517b8430305c1e6149f0977a83d1d3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: idumych <idumych@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:08:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 02/11] Haiku: native interface and BBitmap video output by
 default

Bring back the BeOS interface of VLC 0.x (removed in 2010) as the
"haiku" interface module, and make the Haiku video output native-only:

* libvlccore owns a refcounted BApplication (vlc_haiku_app_Hold/Release)
  so that interface, video and audio plugins work without Qt, and reuses
  the host's be_app when LibVLC is embedded.
* modules/gui/haiku: menu bar, seek slider, transport buttons, volume
  slider and LCD, playlist and messages windows, Open Location, discs,
  subtitles, speed, fullscreen and always-on-top; files dropped or opened
  from Tracker are played.
* video_output/haiku: frames are decoded into source-size BBitmaps and
  scaled by app_server ("BBitmap output"), with fullscreen, on-top,
  keyboard, mouse and double-click support; preferred over OpenGL.
* audio_output/haiku: holds the application, keeps volume and mute
  across streams, no longer resets the volume on start, and no longer
  frees its state twice when BSoundPlayer fails.
* access/dvdnav: on Haiku, only probe folders that are or contain
  VIDEO_TS; libdvdread crashed while scanning ordinary folders, so
  dropping a folder of videos crashed VLC.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
