From 942b756ee04b33fefaad4a284079f55a714dc2f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: idumych <idumych@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:49:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] Haiku interface: the modern (VLC 3) interface in Haiku
 views

--haiku-interface=modern (or Preferences, or View > Classic Interface /
Window > Modern Interface, which switch live and resume a playing video)
gives VLC 3's main window rebuilt with the Interface Kit: menu bar, the
video in the window, seek bar and controls, docked playlist, fullscreen
controller, right-click menu, Media and Codec Information. Classic stays
the default.

The interface module provides a "vout window" of the new type
VOUT_WINDOW_TYPE_HAIKU, whose handle is a BView; the BBitmap and OpenGL
outputs add their view to it, and make their own window as before when
no modern window takes the video.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
